# Roots that are knowingly NOT on the shared R2 backend, one path per line.
# Either form works — `zones/mctl-ru` or `infrastructure/cloudflare/zones/mctl-ru`
# — and an entry naming no real root stops the drift run rather than quietly
# excepting nothing. See .github/scripts/cloudflare-local-state-roots.sh.
#
# Every other root must declare `backend "s3"`, and cloudflare-plan.yml enforces
# that twice: the coverage guard requires a backend.tf to exist, and the plan job
# checks what OpenTofu actually resolved after init — `.terraform/terraform.tfstate`
# records `backend.type`, which no comment or dead block can fake.
#
# A root listed here plans against empty local state on a fresh runner, so its
# plan says nothing about what is live in Cloudflare and drift cannot watch it.
# That is a gap, not a configuration style; the list exists so the gap is
# visible in the gate rather than absent from it.
#
# Empty as of #1178: mctl-ru, mctl-me and mctl-ai all moved onto the shared R2
# backend, which is the last of the exceptions this list ever named. An empty
# list is this file's normal end state, not a sign it should be deleted — the
# three consumers named above still read it, so the next exception, if any, is
# declared here rather than worked around.
